      "cat-harness:section": "Name the instrument that produced the list — bean `pesg`",
      "prov:value": "Two of the\nthree were **live previews for open pull requests #1337 and #914**, which a\nreviewer could have been reading.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1337",
        "#914"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Name the instrument that produced the list — bean `pesg`",
      "prov:value": "`stagingSlug` was exported from `schemas/sdlc/staging.ts` at the time, and\n`test/health/checks.test.ts` already asserted it differentially against the real\n`sed` pipeline. A correct, tested implementation was one import away. So the gap\nwas never duplication in the code — it was that nothing required the list's\nprovenance to be stated."
